msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:117
msgid "Prompt at Launch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:119
msgid ""
"Some options used to configure your deployments have the related option "
"of **Prompt at Launch** in Ansible Tower, which should be enabled on the "
"template to be chosen in the **Job Template** field.  If **Prompt at "
"Launch** is not enabled, the values configured on the template in Ansible"
" Tower will be used instead. **Prompt at Launch** can be seen below on "
"the **Inventory** and **Limit** fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:122
msgid ""
".. image:: "
"/images/integration_guides/automation/ansibleTower/ansibleTowerPromptAtLaunch.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:127
msgid ""
"The **Group** field is optional but a group can be entered into the field"
" to associate the host to, in the target inventory.  If the group is "
"existing, then the instance will be associated as a host to that group.  "
"If the group does not exist, the group will be created and the instance "
"will be associated as a host to that group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:129
msgid ""
".. image:: "
"/images/integration_guides/automation/ansibleTower/ansibleTowerGroups.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:134
msgid ""
"When provisioning on a cloud with a configured Ansible Tower integration "
"or using an Ansible Tower task type against an instance, the instance "
"will be added as a host to the inventory chosen in the **Inventory** "
"field.  As mentioned, if specified, these instance will be associated "
"with groups in the inventory as well. When using an inventory that syncs "
"from a project, the instance will still be added as a host in the "
"inventory, in addition to the sync'd inventory.  This means that Ansible "
"Tower will aggregate the manually added hosts from |morpheus| with the "
"sync'd project inventory. However, if the **Overwrite** option is enabled"
" on the source for the project that contains the inventory, any hosts "
"added by |morpheus| **will be overwritten**.  In some cases, a separate "
"|morpheus| inventory may be desired, if **Overwrite** is required on your"
" sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:138
msgid ""
".. image:: "
"/images/integration_guides/automation/ansibleTower/ansibleTowerOverwrite.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:141
msgid "Passing extra_vars to Ansible Tower Job"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:143
msgid ""
"When provisioning or when running Ansible Tower Jobs as |morpheus| Tasks,"
" you may pass the ``extra_vars`` stack to the Tower Job. First, ensure "
"the Job Template has extra variables \"Prompt on Launch\" enabled as "
"shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:145
msgid ".. image:: /images/automation/towerExtraVars.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:147
msgid "The sample Playbook below is associated with the Tower Job Template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:149
msgid ""
"---\n"
"- hosts: all\n"
"vars:\n"
"  Opensource_Team: \"Customer\"\n"
"tasks:\n"
"- name: Print Hello World\n"
"  debug:\n"
"    msg:\n"
"    - \"Hello World {{ Opensource_Team }}. Here are Morpheus extra_vars: "
"{{ morpheus }}\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:161
msgid ""
"After executing the Tower Job, we can see the variable stack surfaced "
"into the results as defined in the Playbook:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:163
msgid ".. image:: /images/automation/towerResults.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:166
msgid "Use Case"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:168
msgid ""
"You have Job template(s) in Ansible Tower to do post build config after "
"the OS is deployed. The playbook with roles and tasks to do post build "
"will add specific users and groups, install required packages, remove "
"packages, disable services, change config for ntp, resolv, hosts etc. You"
" want to add the instance to an existing Group/Inventory in Tower."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:170
msgid ""
"You can achieve this by adding the Ansible Tower Integration and then "
"scope it to a Cloud or Group. While provisioning an instance, in the "
"config stage you have the Ansible Tower section with option to select the"
" post build job template, select the Inventory and provide an existing "
"Group Name or if the Group doesn't exist Morpheus will create it and "
"submit for provisioning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:172
msgid ""
"Morpheus will provision the instance, once it is in the finalize state "
"where the instance has an ip and has completed domain join if required, "
"added user(s) or User Groups if specified then |morpheus| will add the "
"instance to the inventory and Group and run the Template which will do "
"all the post build of the server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Automation/AnsibleTower.rst:174
msgid ""
"The output of the post build template execution can be see under Instance"
" history."
msgstr ""

